## Context

Ticket 0593 was ruled a monster on 2026-09-02 and is now the tracker for the
attachment-format estate. This is its measurement child: it drives ticket 0599's
matrix through a real Zotero, records what Zotero does with each format, and
puts the candidate policy to the author with every observed exception.

It is the sign-off unit of the estate. Everything before it is authorship and
everything after it implements a ruling, so nothing here may be inferred: what
Zotero exposes for a `.md` attachment, whether RTF reaches `/fulltext` at all,
and what terminal state an unsupported body reports are facts to be observed,
one row at a time.

## This requires a live, idle Zotero, and must not be run beside a build

The local API is single-tenant in practice: a full-library build owns it for the
duration, and the page-cap lift of 2026-09-02 was itself scheduled around one.
Do not start this while any build, census or extraction run holds Zotero's local
API, and do not run it against a Zotero the author is using. The measurement
imports nine records and reindexes them; on a busy instance the reindex queue
alone makes the terminal states unreadable.

The plugin and client are `bench/zotero-fulltext-plugin/` and
`bench/zotero_fulltext.py`; group-library items answer only under the group path
and the plugin resolves keys across libraries.

## The candidate policy, verbatim from ticket 0593

This is the thing being tested. It is stated once, here, and the tracker points
at it rather than repeating it.

- Eligibility follows detected MIME/content capability, never filename
  extension alone.
- PDF uses Zotero text plus the ruled pdf.js structure/page path.
- EPUB and HTML initially use Zotero-extracted flat text; source-aware structure
  is separate measured work.
- Plain text enters directly. TXT and Markdown are probed separately because a
  `.md` attachment need not be exposed as `text/plain`.
- DOC, DOCX, ODT and RTF remain metadata-searchable when Zotero supplies no body
  text, with the stored reason `unsupported-format` rather than an unexplained
  absence or a false indexed state.
- A future local converter needs a separate ruling over security, resource
  budgets, fidelity and derivation identity. Remote conversion is never an
  implicit fallback under R10.

Primary platform reference:
`https://www.zotero.org/support/preferences/search`.

## Actions

1. Import each fixture of ticket 0599's matrix through normal Zotero with
   ordinary record metadata, and record the attachment content type Zotero
   reports.
2. Ask Zotero to reindex each, and probe `/fulltext` plus the full-text control
   plugin's state.
3. Record for each fixture: extension, reported MIME type, whether Zotero
   exposes body text, whether the unique token survives, and the observed
   terminal state. Commit the raw responses and the fixture hashes as evidence
   under `bench/results/`.
4. Put the candidate policy to the author with every observed exception, and
   land the ruling in `DECISIONS.md`. Nothing is written to `SPEC.md` here.

## The open item inherited from ticket 0599

There is no `.doc` fixture. Legacy `.doc` is an OLE2 compound binary that cannot
be synthesized faithfully from bytes, and ticket 0593 authorizes no converter to
produce one. The row must be settled one of two ways, and which one is a
decision to put to the author with the rest:

- a real `.doc` is supplied from outside the repository, and the row is measured
  like every other; or
- the row is ruled on the format's documented behaviour, with the absence of a
  measurement recorded beside the ruling rather than left to look like one.

Report a state that could not be produced as not-produced, never as a negative
observation.

## Verification

- [ ] The raw Zotero responses and the fixture hashes are committed as evidence.
- [ ] Markdown and RTF are classified by observation, not assumption.
- [ ] Every row records the reported MIME type beside ticket 0599's
      content-derived classification, and every disagreement between the two is
      named. A disagreement is the interesting result, not an error.
- [ ] The `.doc` row states which of the two settlements above it took.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check` pass.

## Invariants

Inherited from tracker 0593 and not restated there:

- No converter joins the default path by implication, and no measurement here
  installs LibreOffice, Pandoc, Tika or a cloud converter.
- No network document-conversion service is contacted.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The nine-format matrix is measured, one row per format, with the `.doc`
      row settled explicitly.
- [ ] The author ratifies the attachment-format policy in `DECISIONS.md`,
      including every exception the measurement found.
- [ ] The ruled vocabulary for the extraction route and the unsupported reason
      is fixed by that entry, so ticket 0601 has names to implement.
